          %h3#ForQuasicoherentSheaves Quasicoherent sheaves of modules
          %p
            Pull-push of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quasicoherent+sheaves"} quasicoherent sheaves
            is usually discussed as a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grothendieck+context"} Grothendieck context
            of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/six+operations"} six operations
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Wirthm%C3%BCller+context"} Wirthmüller context
            and hence an indexed monoidal
            = succeed "-category" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
          %p
            Using results of Lurie this follows in the full generality of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/E-%E2%88%9E+geometry"} E-∞ geometry
            (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spectral+geometry"}> spectral geometry
            ).
          %p
            Consider quasi-compact and quasi-separated
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/E-%E2%88%9E+scheme"} E-∞ algebraic spaces
            (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spectral+geometry"}> spectral algebraic spaces
            ). (This includes precisely those
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spectral+Deligne-Mumford+stacks"} spectral Deligne-Mumford stacks
            which have a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/scallop+decomposition"} scallop decomposition
            = succeed ".)" do
              %a{:href => "derived+Deligne-Mumford+stack#RelationToDerivedAlgebraicSpaces"} here
          %p
            If
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi X
                  %mo ⟶
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f \;\colon\; X \longrightarrow Y
            is a map between these which is
          %ol
            %li
              %p locally almost of finite presentation;
            %li
              %p strongly proper;
            %li
              %p
                has finite
                %span.newWikiWord
                  Tor-amplitude
                  %a{:href => "/nlab/new/Tor-amplitude"} ?
          %p
            then the left adjoint to pullback of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quasicoherent+sheaves"} quasicoherent sheaves
            exists
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi f
                    %mo !
                  %mo ⊣
                  %msup
                    %mi f
                    %mo *
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi QCoh
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mover
                    %munder
                      %mo ⟵
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi f
                          %mo *
                    %mover
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi f
                          %mo !
                  %mi QCoh
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  (f_! \dashv f^\ast)
                  \\;\colon\;
                  QCoh(X)
                  \\stackrel{\overset{f_!}{\longrightarrow}}{\underset{f^\ast}{\longleftarrow}}
