                  %mo ⊗
                  %mi B
                  %mo ⟶
                  %msub
                    %mi f
                    %mo *
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo ⊗
                  %msup
                    %mi f
                    %mo *
                  %mi B
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  f_\ast A \otimes B \longrightarrow f_\ast (A\otimes f^\ast B)
          %p
            for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
            quasi-compact and quasi-separated appears as (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Proper+Morphisms%2C+Completions%2C+and+the+Grothendieck+Existence+Theorem"}> LurieProper, remark 1.3.14
            ).
